{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1277319-getting-across-the-inhumanity","id":1277319,"title":"Getting Across the Inhumanity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-29T02:37:18-08:00","id":1277319,"title":"Getting Across the Inhumanity","content":"I'm running a crossover chronicle and was wondering how to get across the sheer inhumanity of... everyone. Kithain, kinain, Gallain, chimera. Everybody. So far, our Prodigal friends have been felled by hungry grass -- &quot;keep off the grass&quot; signs are there for a reason! -- freaked out Garou by having the redcap kinain nip an ear; freak out the vampires by conjuring true fire; swallowed fomori body parts in order to use willow whisper and shed the wyrm taint; eaten a human body in order to get rid of evidence; handled Holy Relics and walked on Holy Ground without any ill effect, and go utterly berserk in combat and (try) to eat my opponent. Not something that works when you don't have teeth.<br /> <br /> I've been using Kithbook Redcaps, the Changeling Player's Guide, Shadow Court, Autumn Nightmares for Lost and The Fair Folk for Exalted. Is there anything else I could use?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T07:11:44-08:00","id":1277355,"title":"","content":"Hmm, you could draw attention to the fact that since the Changeling Way allows the Fey to reincarnate itself into a new host, they have significantly less fear of death than the other prodigals?<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Oh, they died? Don't worry, we'll be seeing them again in about 6 to 10 years, now help me saw this guy's legs off!&quot; - </i>Your Redcap <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-29-2018, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T13:22:02-08:00","id":1277392,"title":"","content":"Weakness to church bells on a throwback old Fae, or salt or some other culture ritual may be worth showing.<br /> <br /> And Sluagh sleeping in a basement of a Library on a moth and water rotted bed, sipping moldy tea?<br /> <br /> Ohhh also Boogies eating poop or urine as a their flaw!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T16:22:00-08:00","id":1277413,"title":"","content":"We hunt down, skin and eat alive BSDs for fun on Samhain. ^^ I've had bogies cause crib death by sucking the breath from young children. Others suck blood from their veins and disdain the vampires. A bunch of Thallain kinain breached the local Technocrat Construct and killed everyone . They made off with nanotech, someone's sidearm and the owner's arm. Some have to count grains of salt spilled across their path, others kill human traffickers for messing with their kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","user":"Saint Michael","date":". 12-29-2018, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T19:04:28-08:00","id":1277427,"title":"","content":"Honestly I use the Seelie stuff to play up the fact that fae aren't playing by the same rules as everyone else. Mostly because people short hand the &quot;light, beauty summer&quot; with &quot;Good&quot;. Unseelie being monsters is pretty par for the course so I find it doesn't shock so much in crossovers.. but when that cute little Disneyesque princess fae burns down a church because the saint it was named after slighted her before the shattering and &quot;NEVER FORGET DEBT&quot; comes into play? That brings home the strange. When harvest glamour from Nazis and other hate groups? Musing them into rants about a glorious &quot;Pure&quot; future? When they help someone stalk a woman because &quot;love conquers all&quot;<br /> <br /> Everyone Expects the Thallain to be monsters. No one is going to bat much of an Eye when they do things to other &quot;bad&quot; groups. Use the Seelie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T20:20:36-08:00","id":1277437,"title":"","content":"That's one thing I'm really hoping from the new Players Guide. C20 did way too much to reenforce the misconception that &quot;Seelie = Good, Unseelie = Bad&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T20:31:31-08:00","id":1277439,"title":"","content":"Better yet, try to keep in mind the fairy tales about how the Fey chose to punish people for their misdeeds. In almost every instance, the punishment they delivered would be described as &quot;cruel and unusual&quot; by any modern interpretation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Remember, the Fey don't just emulate humanity's dreams, they ARE humanity's dreams. <br /> <br /> The Sidhe ARE perfection, the Satyrs ARE passion, the Redcaps ARE hunger.<br /> <br /> So, when showing off Changelings to the other prodigals, make a point to emphasize that they are dealing with a creature who embodies the ideals of humanity's collective imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-30T09:27:27-08:00","id":1277514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1277319-getting-across-the-inhumanity?p=1277437#post1277437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's one thing I'm really hoping from the new Players Guide. C20 did way too much to reenforce the misconception that &quot;Seelie = Good, Unseelie = Bad&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think they did a better job than previous editions. I think the bigger issue to get across monsterousness of Kithain is that Glamour/Banality doesn't map to Good and Bad. The Sundering and Shattering happened because humanity chose Banality as a good thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-30T23:04:56-08:00","id":1277610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1277319-getting-across-the-inhumanity?p=1277437#post1277437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's one thing I'm really hoping from the new Players Guide. C20 did way too much to reenforce the misconception that &quot;Seelie = Good, Unseelie = Bad&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, judging from the previews, we are confirmed to get Seelie Ravaging and Unseelie Musing Thresholds. Seems like a step in the right direction to that end.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T08:44:07-08:00","id":1278081,"title":"","content":"I can confirm that both Pete and I do not adhere to the \u201cSeelie=good, Unseelie=bad\u201d interpretation. In my personal games, I don\u2019t even limit Legacies by Seelie or Unseelie. You can be a Seelie monster the same as you can be an Unseelie champion. The difference is in perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T09:05:23-08:00","id":1278085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luka C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1277319-getting-across-the-inhumanity?p=1278081#post1278081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can confirm that both Pete and I do not adhere to the \u201cSeelie=good, Unseelie=bad\u201d interpretation. In my personal games, I don\u2019t even limit Legacies by Seelie or Unseelie. You can be a Seelie monster the same as you can be an Unseelie champion. The difference is in perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good. That's how I do it here. I'm just hopeful that the Players Guide will bring that in line more with the text, as that really shapes how players (especially new to me players) perceive the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T13:19:35-08:00","id":1278129,"title":"","content":"Yes, I also found Seelie being good, Unseelie being evil, irritating. My Unseelie sluagh usually asks the motley's opinion on matters -- kinain, Kithain, Prodigal, mortal or otherwise -- and then takes that into account. His Seelie half is.... much more unpleasant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T18:41:07-08:00","id":1278212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luka C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1277319-getting-across-the-inhumanity?p=1278081#post1278081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can confirm that both Pete and I do not adhere to the \u201cSeelie=good, Unseelie=bad\u201d interpretation. In my personal games, I don\u2019t even limit Legacies by Seelie or Unseelie. You can be a Seelie monster the same as you can be an Unseelie champion. The difference is in perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What do legacies represent then? I've always had a strong &quot;society vs freedom&quot; from Seelie and Unseelie so I find it hard to imagine unseelie legacies as Seelie...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T18:53:19-08:00","id":1278214,"title":"","content":"Personally I make the Courts represent the two Codes, plus a political division.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T21:09:50-08:00","id":1278240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1277319-getting-across-the-inhumanity?p=1278214#post1278214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I make the Courts represent the two Codes, plus a political division.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but what do Legacies represent? Why is there two? Why do they &quot;Swap&quot;. I Mean I can easily see members of various legacies holding up the court in theirown way.. but if there's nothing to the seasonal change, to the Division.. why do even the Gallain have such?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T04:05:15-08:00","id":1278282,"title":"","content":"The player picks a legacy to represent their character's Seelie side, and another to represent their Unseelie side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T08:18:18-08:00","id":1278323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luka C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1277319-getting-across-the-inhumanity?p=1278081#post1278081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can confirm that both Pete and I do not adhere to the \u201cSeelie=good, Unseelie=bad\u201d interpretation. In my personal games, I don\u2019t even limit Legacies by Seelie or Unseelie. You can be a Seelie monster the same as you can be an Unseelie champion. The difference is in perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If everybody continued to follow medieval style traditions then the world would be a lot more violent than it is today (looking at you, Redcaps)!<br /> <br /> Unseelie being &quot;bad guys&quot; is just trite propaganda, spat out by the Seelie in order to justify their tyranny!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-03-2019, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T12:05:41-08:00","id":1291899,"title":"","content":"The Legacy division might be a product of the Shattering. Somehow. No one in Dark Ages Fae has Legacies, and the Sundering has already occurred by then. The local redcaps would totally be eating popcorn and watching executions for fun. They might still do it today.... and cause the electric chair to malfunction for laughs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T14:49:06-08:00","id":1291968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saint Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1277319-getting-across-the-inhumanity?p=1291899#post1291899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Legacy division might be a product of the Shattering. Somehow. No one in Dark Ages Fae has Legacies, and the Sundering has already occurred by then. The local redcaps would totally be eating popcorn and watching executions for fun. They might still do it today.... and cause the electric chair to malfunction for laughs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That might be more the work of Goblins, actually.<br /> <br /> A Redcap would probably use the guillotine, who's method of execution was not nearly as swift and painless as we have been lead to believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}